# Goal: boolean transform + cache hygiene (next release)

Add to reportgen:

1. `boolean` transform: rules files may map a column to `boolean`; a value
   is accepted case-insensitively when it is one of yes/no/true/false and
   must be reported as 1.0 for the affirmative forms and 0.0 for the
   negative ones. Any other input raises TransformError, like the other
   numeric transforms.
2. Cache hygiene: a `cache/state.json` written by a future schema version
   (a version field greater than the current REGISTRY_VERSION) must not
